Vulkan per-draw loops and whole-load stats.
- The float constants a shader uses are copied into its constant buffer a run of consecutive constants per memcpy
  instead of one constant at a time, and vertex buffer residency is invalidated a 64-bit mask at a time for runs of
  fetch constants, as 0101 does for D3D12.
- With gpu_frame_stats, the submissions log line also gives the whole process's CPU time per frame (all threads) and
  the host GPU time per frame of the replayed command buffers, from a timestamp at the start and end of each (a slot
  is reused only once its submission has completed and been read), so a frame's limit shows: the GPU command thread,
  the rest of the process, or the GPU. vkCmdWriteTimestamp and vkGetQueryPoolResults join the device function table.

